    <property name="text">
     <string>values create the illusion that the mission is under control. Figure 8-2 shows the GPS visualization interface, allowing teams to track the CanSat’s location in real time and estimate where it may eventually land. Figure 8-3 shows acceleration, gyroscope, and altitude graphs used to analyze flight behavior throughout the mission. Aerospace engineers enjoy graphs because they make even catastrophic failures appear scientific.</string>
